                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4a86a1ee-1f06-3753-9fa3-121f9f1f770f",
                        "entry_id": "a7724169-25aa-32c9-a9b9-4ddea409ac27",
                        "glosses": [
                            "rasa psa charakteryzującego się masywną budową ciała, o pomarszczonym czole i obwisłych uszach"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f85c53b5-1165-4c0f-b428-5b075dc01412",
                        "source_entry_id": "a7724169-25aa-32c9-a9b9-4ddea409ac27",
                        "source_sense_id": "4a86a1ee-1f06-3753-9fa3-121f9f1f770f",
                        "target_lang_word": "mastiff",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mastiff",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d78a5881-72a4-33a8-b06e-01f9e3f3e1e8",
                                        "entry_id": "8fac52d5-e83d-3bea-b41d-5e8efcf3effa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One of an old breed of powerful, deep-chested, and smooth-coated dogs, used chiefly as watchdogs and guard dogs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ef6c67ba-8d8c-4b6c-bdb9-8d1a8f9f5d3a",
                                                "sense_id": "d78a5881-72a4-33a8-b06e-01f9e3f3e1e8",
                                                "text": "At which time, they wryte that Demoſthenes told the people of Athens, the fable of the ſheepe and woulues, how that the woulues came on a time, and willed the ſheepe, if they woulde haue peace with them, to deliuer them their maſtiues that kept them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d0ae167c-a649-4ac6-8b72-f4eff526bd89",
                                                "sense_id": "d78a5881-72a4-33a8-b06e-01f9e3f3e1e8",
                                                "text": "As ſaluage Bull, whom two fierce maſtiues bayt, / When rancour doth with rage him once engore, / Forgets with wary warde them to awayt, / But with his dreadfull hornes them driues afore, / Or flings aloft or treades downe in the flore, / Breathing out wrath, and bellowing diſdaine, / That all the foreſt quakes to heare him rore: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b7bd2f0e-23f3-440d-9d91-8857020d877e",
                                                "sense_id": "d78a5881-72a4-33a8-b06e-01f9e3f3e1e8",
                                                "text": "They fill’d the Capitoll, and Pompei’s Circke: / Where, like ſo many Maſtiues, biting ſtones, / As if his Statues novv vvere ſenſitiue / Of their vvild fury, firſt they teare them dovvne: / Then faſtning ropes, drag them along the ſtreetes, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85cafab3-f3f2-44d3-bd01-99ca801388e7",
                                                "sense_id": "d78a5881-72a4-33a8-b06e-01f9e3f3e1e8",
                                                "text": "Avaunt, you curs! Be thy mouth or black or white, Tooth that poisons if it bite; Mastiff, greyhound, mongrel grim, Hound or spaniel, brach or him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bbffd8f2-7cf0-49fb-bcc8-c6362c84922a",
                                                "sense_id": "d78a5881-72a4-33a8-b06e-01f9e3f3e1e8",
                                                "text": "The conquering foe they soon assail’d; / First Trulla stav’d, and Cerdon tail’d, / Until their Mastives loos’d their hold: / And yet alas! do what they could, / The worsted Bear came off with store / Of bloudy wounds, but all before."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "805caa99-9d5f-46de-be18-8a3bc4bb97d4",
                                                "sense_id": "d78a5881-72a4-33a8-b06e-01f9e3f3e1e8",
                                                "text": "Soon as Ulyſſes near th’encloſure drew, / With open mouths the furious maſtives flew: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f6296ee-435d-4a5c-a581-3ca383b204e6",
                                                "sense_id": "d78a5881-72a4-33a8-b06e-01f9e3f3e1e8",
                                                "text": "Her, who did erst the lengthened fight maintain, / And heaped the death-pile red with Prankish gore, / The Vert fangs now to vassalage constrain: / The mastives old and young, Verrucchio bore, / Who in their lawless rule Montagna slew, / Make their teeth augres where they wont of yore: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f9b7b8d0-1271-476f-afee-49fd4b87ef61",
                                                "sense_id": "d78a5881-72a4-33a8-b06e-01f9e3f3e1e8",
                                                "text": "The Mastiff is a good fighter, and can kill a wildcat, taking the necessary punishment well, as we found out when we once trapped one of these small lynxes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d3f08aa-ea20-4d71-a43b-10845298cde7",
                                                "sense_id": "d78a5881-72a4-33a8-b06e-01f9e3f3e1e8",
                                                "text": "Neither of them could say how many years it had been since the week-long poisoning epidemic, which first took their father’s bulls, then his mastives, then the man himself; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2f9268d4-29a8-4676-9533-69ed24e3e09c",
                                                "sense_id": "d78a5881-72a4-33a8-b06e-01f9e3f3e1e8",
                                                "text": "Milei’s allies reject his portrayal as an unbalanced powder keg, although they do not refute claims their leader takes counsel from his cloned mastiffs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c295b67d-0a54-4180-a2ae-e08e8ce196d8",
